      </div>

      <div class="job">
        <div class="job-head"><span class="job-co">Cortex</span><span class="job-role">Principal Product Designer</span><span class="job-when">May 2025 &ndash; Dec 2025</span></div>
        <p>Cortex is an engineering intelligence platform: a catalog of every service a company runs, scorecards for how healthy they are, and the dashboards engineering leaders use to decide what to fix. I was the principal designer, working on how engineering teams adopt it and keep using it.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="job">
        <div class="job-head"><span class="job-co">Labelbox</span><span class="job-role">VP of Design &larr; Head of Design &larr; Principal &larr; Lead</span><span class="job-when">Feb 2020 &ndash; Jun 2025</span></div>
        <p>Joined as the lead designer, ended up VP, stayed hands-on the whole time. Labelbox is a data labeling and model evaluation platform, a complicated product that a lot of people had to learn quickly, so much of the work was making it approachable: onboarding, first-project setup, the free tier, the paths from trying it to buying it, and the workflows that keep teams in it every day. I hired and ran the design team, set the bar for craft, built the design system, and did the reviews, while the whole AI field took off around us.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="job">
        <div class="job-head"><span class="job-co">Metromile</span><span class="job-role">Senior Product Designer</span><span class="job-when">Aug 2019 &ndash; Feb 2020</span></div>
        <p>Designed the fraud-detection tools for Metromile Enterprise: an ML model flags a claim, an investigator decides if it's real. My job was the screen in between.</p>
      </div>

